## Prose

Write one sentence per line.
Break after `。`, `！`, `？`, `.`, `!`, and `?`.
A break after `、`, `,`, `;`, `:`, or an em dash may clarify structure.
Never wrap prose to a column, and never join a paragraph onto one line.
Lines have no length limit.
Never use hard line breaks inside a paragraph.
A blank line separates paragraphs.

The rule covers English and Japanese in Markdown files, code comments, commit messages, issue and PR bodies, and release notes.
Consecutive comment lines form a paragraph, and a trailing comment stands alone.
When editing a column-wrapped paragraph, reflow the whole paragraph in the same change.
